# Frontend TypeScript/React sources are always text, never binary, even if a
# file happens to contain a raw NUL byte (as src/components/Sidebar.tsx once
# did, in a composite-key separator, before it was rewritten as the \x00
# escape). Without this, git's content-sniffing heuristic classifies such a
# file as binary — no diff, no blame, unreadable by a reviewer.
*.ts diff
*.tsx diff
